00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
Turbo is a 2013 American animated sports comedy film directed by David
Soren and written by Soren, Darren Lemke and Robert Siegel.

11
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It stars Ryan Reynolds, Paul Giamatti, Michael Peña, Snoop Dogg,
Maya Rudolph, Michelle Rodriguez, and Samuel L.

12
00:52:21,818 --> 00:52:27,818
In the film, a garden snail pursues his dream of winning the
Indianapolis 500 after a freak accident gives him super speed.

13
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
In 2009, DreamWorks Animation organized a competition for its
staff to submit a one-page pitch for film ideas.

14
01:01:05,454 --> 01:01:11,454
Soren's concept was "The Fast and the Furious with
snails" and he won the competition.

15
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
With no further development for several years, Soren pushed the project again after he
and his family moved into a new home with a backyard infested with snails.

16
01:09:49,090 --> 01:09:55,090
For the racing elements of the film, Soren was inspired
by his son's fascination with race cars.

17
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
Turbo premiered at CineEurope on May 20, 2013, and was theatrically released
in the United States on July 17, 2013, by 20th Century Fox.

18
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
It received mixed reviews from critics.

19
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
Despite earning $282 million on a $127 million budget, the film was a box
office disappointment, and lost the studio $13.5 million.

20
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
A television series based on the film, Turbo Fast, was released in 2013.

21
01:31:38,181 --> 01:31:44,181
The film explores themes of underdog, dreams, car race, sports, speed.
